.TITLE "cd"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Changes the current shell working directory. It is the primary tool for __navigating__ through the filesystem hierarchy and switching between folders.

.DIV "TLDR"
**cd path**
Changes the current directory to the specified path.
> __path__ the target directory

**cd ..**
Moves up one level in the directory tree to the parent folder.
> 

**cd**
Returns to the home directory of the current user.
> 

**cd -**
Returns to the previously occupied directory.
> 

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Using __cd -__ is an efficient way to toggle between two deeply nested folders. If you encounter permissions issues, ensure you have __execute__ permissions for the target directory.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**cli:pwd** **cli:ls** **cli:pushd**

